{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included","id":1522985,"title":"Resources Not Included","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-22T19:29:48-07:00","id":1522985,"title":"Resources Not Included","content":"I like the fact the Resources Background wasn't included in Mage: the Ascension, 2nd Edition; a mage is the closest thing to an enlightened-individual, and the fact they need pursue money, defeats the purpose of the game. If a mage really needs money, if they have Matter, they can, coincidentally find it, Mind, people will give you it, or Entropy, and a slot-machine, they will, &quot;Win&quot;, it. It moves the focus on magical-powers, vs. material-gains, like in V:tM(where you have to posses, a haven, or sun-tan).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T19:50:32-07:00","id":1522986,"title":"","content":"really i agree, but i should point out there's an entire faction that's entirely about money","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T20:29:06-07:00","id":1522990,"title":"","content":"It's not there because 1st and 2nd ed WoD games only allotted enough space for 10 background write ups, and because Mage decided to include things like Avatar, Arcane, Dream, Node, Library, and Destiny, Resources ended up getting bumped to the Players Guide/Book of Shadows alongside other relatively important things like Chantry, Familiar, and Sanctum. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T03:27:06-07:00","id":1523003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1522990#post1522990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not there because 1st and 2nd ed WoD games only allotted enough space for 10 background write ups, and because Mage decided to include things like Avatar, Arcane, Dream, Node, Library, and Destiny, Resources ended up getting bumped to the Players Guide/Book of Shadows alongside other relatively important things like Chantry, Familiar, and Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. And in those early books there was a larger expectation that you'd have the supplements or just crib it from another WoD book if you needed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:58:51-07:00","id":1523024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included#post1522985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the fact the Resources Background wasn't included in Mage: the Ascension, 2nd Edition; a mage is the closest thing to an enlightened-individual, and the fact they need pursue money, defeats the purpose of the game. If a mage really needs money, if they have Matter, they can, coincidentally find it, Mind, people will give you it, or Entropy, and a slot-machine, they will, &quot;Win&quot;, it. It moves the focus on magical-powers, vs. material-gains, like in V:tM(where you have to posses, a haven, or sun-tan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveats with this strategy.<br /> <br /> Conjuring up wealth out of nowhere is going to get the tehcnocracy on your tail, either the Syndicate are going to be on your doorstep to find out where all this new gold came from, especially as such a thing will threaten their controlled economy. Or it will bring the NWO on you since tax evasion laws is a really good way for them to root out mystics who try to live off grid.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say mages don't employ these strategies, it's just that doing so isn't the easy solution you make it out to be. Having Resources means you can get income without needing to cover your tracks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T15:02:45-07:00","id":1523101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included#post1522985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the fact the Resources Background wasn't included in Mage: the Ascension, 2nd Edition; a mage is the closest thing to an enlightened-individual, and the fact they need pursue money, defeats the purpose of the game. If a mage really needs money, if they have Matter, they can, coincidentally find it, Mind, people will give you it, or Entropy, and a slot-machine, they will, &quot;Win&quot;, it. It moves the focus on magical-powers, vs. material-gains, like in V:tM(where you have to posses, a haven, or sun-tan).</div> </div> </div> </div>It also depends on how you interpret the resources' background. In our games, not having resources doesn't mean you are poor or that you don't have any money, it means that you don't have disposable income. Everything you make goes to cover your basic needs (House, food, clothes, transportation, internet, phone, etc...) regardless if you live in a shitty apartment in the poor part of the city or a mansion in the outskirts. Also, sure, a mage can easily make some cash quickly with their magick, but it's not a sustainable strategy in the long term for many reasons (Paradox, technocracy, justyfing revenue, etc). Resources represent a legal, stable, and continuous source of income that the mage can use without worrying too much about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 09-25-2023, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T17:29:23-07:00","id":1523107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523003#post1523003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. And in those early books there was a larger expectation that you'd have the supplements or just crib it from another WoD book if you needed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. When I did my WIR thread about 2nd ed Vampire clanbook templates, it was weird how some clanbook writers would go all out on the secondary abilities from the PG, while others would almost totally ignore them. <br /> <br /> (I really should get around to doing the original tribe and tradition book ones. Some of the original Virtual Adept and Akashic Brotherhood ones were downright bizarre. \ud83e\udd14)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T02:15:43-07:00","id":1523126,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely in the camp of &quot;relying purely on Magick to survive is not sustainable&quot;. If I'm the Storyteller, trying to get out of investing in Resources means you have to play out the act of surviving day to day. ESPECIALLY if you're using Magick to do it. There's a reason street level games, where half the Cabal are homeless, is a style of play unto itself. Just making it through day to day is the challenge, let alone accomplishing anything in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> If you try saying &quot;oh, I just use Magick to feed myself today&quot;, I would respond, &quot;Oh? Okay, tell me what Spheres you use, and roll Arete please.&quot; Over, and over, and over. You are going to wrestle with the possibility of a Botch, the Domino Effect, and Paradox for as long as you try to dodge having one of the basic Backgrounds. Much as if you try to pull strings in the world without having Influence. The point of the Background is to justify just being able to do things without going into too much detail. Without Influence, you have to roleplay out the act of influencing people/systems, including the necessary rolls (and risk) associated with Magick. That's how the game works.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if your character has done enough with their Magick to justify having enough money to obviate basic survival as a factor, by nature of definition they have enough wealth to represent at least one dot of Resources. So it's a distinction without a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T05:12:39-07:00","id":1523129,"title":"","content":"I often gave my mages various dots in resources with the explanation that they were the result of my magick supplying a stable income source (versus a one-off \u201cI need cash now\u201d situation).<br /> <br /> Various explanations were net-hecking to claim some of the rounded off fractions of pennies, phenomenal luck winning me $100 at a time from scratch-offs, visions aiding my stock choices (just not so much as to make the SEC suspicious), or alchemically creating gold and selling it a fractional ounce at a time for the spot price at pawn shops.<br /> <br /> My favorite was borrowed from the Order of Hermes trad book involving a ritual circle of seven credit cards marked with arcane sigils into which that month\u2019s bills were places and then digital spirits it summoned would basically go and do the net-hack thing of gathering fractional cents to settle the balances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T12:36:13-07:00","id":1523143,"title":"","content":"Given that Magick can gather resources most mages would have some level of the <b>Resources </b>background. The process of gathering those resources is inherently risky. So the average intelligent Mage would build up their resources and then play more or less by reality's rules. How many resources you gather involves several different factors.<br /> <br /> Knowing how to quietly manage resources is an issue. Mages don't want to much attention.<br /> <br /> On another thread I mentioned a Cult of Ecstasy mage that had a small jazz record label. It basically allows him to support a few good musicians and offer some artists the opportunity to design album covers. The Cultist would rather live like people think Rock Stars live. But between paradox and the Technocracy, the Cultist settles for middle class comfort and achieving some goals they care about. <br /> <br /> An Heremetic who comes from old money can set up more lavish conditions for their lifestyle and pass relatively unnoticed. But much of the plausibility of their position comes from their family background. They are the sort of person you'd expect to have a trust fund.<br /> <br /> For mages the <b>Resources </b>background is a matter of their general background. A working-class person with <b>Resources 5</b> will excite curiosity and not just among the Technocracy. Mages keep their heads down to work on their larger goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-25-2023, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T13:58:46-07:00","id":1523146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523126#post1523126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you try saying &quot;oh, I just use Magick to feed myself today&quot;, I would respond, &quot;Oh? Okay, tell me what Spheres you use, and roll Arete please.&quot; </div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me that someone I used to game with came up with the idea of a somewhat common talisman called The Lunch Box. They were made from those metal lunch boxes from the 70s and 80s, and having one with a &quot;cool&quot; character/show was a point of social prestige, especially for Hollow Ones. Every day, at noon, it would produce a small meal for one. Typically a kid's sandwich, some sort of side (frequently fruit), and a carton of milk or juice. It was usually the same thing everyday, but about once a week it was something different as a treat.<br /> These were mainly a thing for twenty-something Gen X mages (our games usually defaulting to the early 90s) but I could easily see doing something similar with, say, an antique upper class picnic basket.<br /> <br /> I wish I could remember how many background points it cost. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T00:24:47-07:00","id":1523164,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, like any other game, you can make money as relevant as you want it to be. I understand your frustration, I share your preference, a mage should be out there having adventures in their eternal quest for ascension and not wasting time about how they're going to pay the rent. That's why my approach is that resources decide how much extra cash you make, not whether or not you have any income at all. That said, there's nothing inherently wrong about games where mages have to deal with more mundane issues if that's what you want. It's all about what kind of game you want to play and what issues you wish to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T08:31:38-07:00","id":1523177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523164#post1523164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, like any other game, you can make money as relevant as you want it to be. I understand your frustration, I share your preference, a mage should be out there having adventures in their eternal quest for ascension and not wasting time about how they're going to pay the rent. That's why my approach is that resources decide how much extra cash you make, not whether or not you have any income at all. That said, there's nothing inherently wrong about games where mages have to deal with more mundane issues if that's what you want. It's all about what kind of game you want to play and what issues you wish to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your approach is RAW as of M20. No dots is \u201cyou live paycheck-to-paycheck, and that\u2019s about it\u201d which does imply you have a way of making money, but it immediately goes back out into your living expenses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T15:07:56-07:00","id":1523189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523024#post1523024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caveats with this strategy.<br /> <br /> Conjuring up wealth out of nowhere is going to get the tehcnocracy on your tail, either the Syndicate are going to be on your doorstep to find out where all this new gold came from, especially as such a thing will threaten their controlled economy. Or it will bring the NWO on you since tax evasion laws is a really good way for them to root out mystics who try to live off grid.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say mages don't employ these strategies, it's just that doing so isn't the easy solution you make it out to be. Having Resources means you can get income without needing to cover your tracks</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't any magik a Council mage does attract the Technocracy? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T17:05:30-07:00","id":1523190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523189#post1523189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't any magik a Council mage does attract the Technocracy?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not every magick, but any magick. Which is why I assume that the average non Technocracy mage would chose some level of subtly. Carefully use coincidental magick to build a nest egg of some type, then live quietly on that nest egg while you work on bigger projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T00:46:10-07:00","id":1523198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523189#post1523189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't any magik a Council mage does attract the Technocracy?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Only if that magick causes a big enough disruption to a system. For example, if city pawn shops are suddenly inundated with objects made out of gold, that will draw the attention of the technocracy. Any action that would have a significant impact on the economy of a city or a region in a short period of time really. That's why smart mages only use magick to get cash quickly very occasionally or in an emergency. This doesn't mean you can't use Magick to get resources, it just means that you must do it slowly and subtly over a long period of time to not attract attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T02:25:18-07:00","id":1523200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523198#post1523198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if that magick causes a big enough disruption to a system. For example, if city pawn shops are suddenly inundated with objects made out of gold, that will draw the attention of the technocracy. Any action that would have a significant impact on the economy of a city or a region in a short period of time really. That's why smart mages only use magick to get cash quickly very occasionally or in an emergency. This doesn't mean you can't use Magick to get resources, it just means that you must do it slowly and subtly over a long period of time to not attract attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also smart mages change tactics. If last week I sold off some gold rings, then this week I'll use coincidental Magick to &quot;find&quot; some rare comic books from the 60s or the 40s in mint condition. Or maybe I'll have a complete set of carnival glass. The smart mage doesn't coincidentally &quot;find&quot; ACTION #1. They find a few comic books that can sell 50 to 100 dollars each. Nothing that would make the news. First editions of Dickens or Twain? No! Rare to find OZ books or a Margaret Murry 1st ed? Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T08:02:43-07:00","id":1523415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included#post1522985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the fact the Resources Background wasn't included in Mage: the Ascension, 2nd Edition; a mage is the closest thing to an enlightened-individual, and the fact they need pursue money, defeats the purpose of the game. If a mage really needs money, if they have Matter, they can, coincidentally find it, Mind, people will give you it, or Entropy, and a slot-machine, they will, &quot;Win&quot;, it. It moves the focus on magical-powers, vs. material-gains, like in V:tM(where you have to posses, a haven, or sun-tan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck convincing the IRS that you just found a pile of gold buried in your garden.<br /> <br /> And, after failing to convince the IRS, you can be sure that you won't convince their superiors at the &quot;FBI&quot; - oh wait, they are actually NWO MiBs... Ready to send you to room 101...<br /> <br /> So yeah, while it is fine to conjure a few bucks in order to get your groceries, trying to get all the expensive and exotic materials that you need on a constant basis to fuel the entirety of your lab by just simply conjuring gold from your basement will eventually cause you some troubles.<br /> <br /> That's what the Resources background is for. It's a legitimate source of income that don't rely on &quot;cripto-magic&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T08:55:02-07:00","id":1523423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522985-resources-not-included?p=1523189#post1523189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't any magik a Council mage does attract the Technocracy?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of ways to use Magik to &quot;climb the social ladder&quot; without attracting unwanted attention - and I don't mean just the Techies here. People forget that besides the boys in black, there's also the good ol' government (IRS may want a word with you), the Nefandi is always looking for promising recruits, if you look yourself too talented you may inadvertently attracting the attention of a Venture or Tremere elder that, not knowing any better, mistakes you for a solid prospect for the Embrace, and many many other threats.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b Despite all of that, there's still many ways to climb the social ladder without attracting unwanted attention. Mind 2 is probably your best friend here - people likes you. &quot;John? Yeah, he's just such a cool guy... I just feel such a good vibe from him...&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind 2 is almost a garantee that you would pass in ANY job interview ever. After that, Mind 2 is still your best friend in helping you climb the corporate ladder, since it will be your ticket towards promotion by being the &quot;favorite of the boss&quot;. Mind 2 will also help you by quenching the inevitable flames of envy that otherwise would surely by fanning your way.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 and/or Entropy 1 will help you discern which people to trust and which to be wary of at work or businesses. That's another great help, and Mind 2 will dissuade those that would want to become obstacles for your rise.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 is also your friend when trying to recruit employees; use it in order to garantee that you'll get the best talented people possible for your business.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 can also be used for &quot;playing dice&quot; at the stocks market... The problem here is that gamblers have no self control. If your mage knew when to quit, that would be good, but gamblers NEVER know when to quit. Most likely than not the Mage would &quot;do it just one more time&quot;, becoming a millionaire over night and winning a one way ticket to a 101 room. But, if you are smart and have self control, you could use that in order to have a small extra income every month.<br /> <br /> The problem with using Entropy 1 to play with stocks is a problem of math too. So, I'd suggest having a good dose of Financial skills so that you can PRETEND to be doing it organically rather than magically - aka sometimes you have to lose in order to win.<br /> <br /> But, if you have Finances 4 or 5, why would you need Magik for? That's another question you'd have to answer.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 can also be used in order to start a new business. For example, take a map of the city you live in, make a list with the 10 small businesses types that would have higher chance of success in the town (use Entropy 1 for that), and then use Entropy 1 again to choose the best spots to settle any single one of those businesses. For example, you could do this in order to get the best spot for opening a bakery in your neighborhood, and just by doing that almost garantees that your small bakery will be a tremendous success.<br /> <br /> Use Entropy 1 to &quot;smell&quot; opportunities, to &quot;fish&quot; for the best suppliers for example.<br /> <br /> Mind 2 would make all your costumers simply love your bakery (&quot;I feel absolutely at home in &quot;Bread&amp;Bread&quot;, I love that place).<br /> <br /> With Mind 1/Entropy 1 you find a guy that is super honest and competent enough to be the manager for you, and all your employees are dedicated and hard working. And you may even a small dose of Mind 2 to make them all extra loyal and extra dedicated to you.<br /> <br /> After a while doing this, you can set a second bakery, then a third, a fourth and a fifth... And after that, you'll let your manager become the &quot;CEO&quot; of your franchise and you'll stop using Magik to improve your business all together, because at that point you'd start to get the risk of drawing attention, and honestly, at this point you no longer need to use Magik to boost it, you can let your business grow organically by itself because it has already being built on solid foundations (you already have the contacts, the best suppliers, loyal costumers to make mouth to mouth advertising, the best locations, loyal, capable and dedicated employees and so on).<br /> <br /> Or you could have a farm and use Life 1 to select the seeds for your crops, doing that for a while and you'll achieve incredible wields over time.<br /> <br /> Just don't be &quot;incredible lucky&quot; all the time and don't show a meteoric rise from rags to riches, and ideally, build a solid foundation using Magik on very small doses and in concealed ways, but when you move from &quot;small&quot; to &quot;medium&quot;, drop Magik use all together and just go naturally - or just use some modicum doses of Magik, like for example using little bits of Entropy 1 to give a small edge on Finance or Administration skills (particularly if you do NOT naturally have those skills).<br /> <br /> Now, if you're living on the streets, conjuring a few hundreds of bucks for buying groceries is fine. Nobody pays attention to everybody going in and out of supermarkets, that won't raise suspicions, even if you do it daily. The problem of that is that you'll live and die by your Magik - get ready to face many botches and tons of paradox if you rely on conjuring money on a daily basis.<br /> <br /> The worse use of Magik to get rich is probably Matter. Yeah, conjure gold.<br /> <br /> One problem is: &quot;fools' gold&quot;.<br /> <br /> When your spell duration ends... The gold vanishes.<br /> <br /> And that's a problem because, the pawn house you sold your gold too, eventually they'll realize they have been duped. And they'll call the police. And the MiBs will answer the phone when the guy says that &quot;I dunno what he did, but I'm telling you man, the gold he sold me just turned into mud, I don't know how he did it but that guy duped me!&quot;<br /> <br /> Either that or the guy will call the organized crime local boss. In which case, eventually that story about &quot;gold turning into mud&quot; will end up in the ears of a Syndicate Enforcer. And then, you're screwed.<br /> <br /> You could make the spell permanent. Yeah, but that's harder. But ok.<br /> <br /> Now, selling a few grams of gold every now and then is fine, but do it too much and inevitably either the police or the local mobsters will invariably know on your door. And eventually, either an Enforcer or MiB will get in your trail.<br /> <br /> So, those are the ways to get ahead in life using Magik and not ending up a prisoner in Mecha II or being embraced by a vampire or throw into a Nefandic labyrinth...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}